			"notes": "Builds for Minecraft 26.3 and 26.2.\n\nPick the jar that matches your Minecraft version. SHA-256 sums are in SHA256SUMS.txt.\n\nChanges\n- Added GitHub build and tag release workflows\n- Documented the new modules and the privacy notice\n- Added 26.2 and 26.3 builds from one source tree with per-version update manifests\n- Fixed shader sources, mixins and mouse buttons for 26.3\n- Ported the client to the 26.3 render, input and auth APIs\n- Merged Friends, Accounts, Waypoints, Download, Nametags, Deaths and Swing Trails into host modules\n- Added DonutSMP region overlay, Explore page, chunk previews, faster live sharing and unlimited zoom out\n- Added shared live maps with friends, per-friend location and faster map saving\n- Added live nearest-first block search and gear icons on player cards\n- Added block search, player heads and cards, 3D map setting and lighter chunk loading\n- Fixed fog hiding explored areas on the map\n- Fixed block sides, floating platforms, water under overhangs and slow loading\n- Added overhangs, cloud sea and teleport glide, fixed Nether shutdown\n- Added 3D map view and mob head icons\n- Fixed water colour, clipping and cloud pops, added mobs and 3D blocks\n- Added map, minimap and world download modules\n- Added place and break styles and fixed beds, torches and block entities\n- Added restyling for text display holograms\n- Fixed trails cutting off on flip swings and their hard edges\n- Added swing trails with five styles for first and third person\n- Fixed entity effects staying visible behind walls\n- Fixed invisible and glitching block animations and the outline following them\n- Fixed own messages being hidden by the chat filter\n- Changed Friends System\n- Added live window mirror element with Windows, X11 and Wayland capture\n- Added entity models, animation and states\n- Added texture pack mixer with version picker and Modrinth\n- Initial release"
		}
